n Projections.","3. Starting January 2026, the 2020 Census of Population and Housing Population Projections was used.","4. Starting April 2005, the new unemployment definition was adopted per NSCB Resolution no. 15 dated October 20, 2004. As indicated in the said resolution, the unemployed include all persons who are 15 years old and over as of their last birthday and are reported as (1) without work; AND (2) currently available for work; AND (3) seeking work OR not seeking work due to valid reasons.","5. The methodology for the computation of annual estimates of labor and employment indicators is based on the Philippine Statistics Authority (PSA) Board Resolution No. 14 Series of 2021 - Adopting the General Method for Annualized Estimates for the Labor Force Survey 2021 and Beyond.","6. The Annual 2025 is based on the official release last March 19, 2026 and is computed based on the preliminary estimates from January 2025 to December 2025.","7. Estimates from January 2023 to August 2025 were final.","8. Estimates from September 2025 to August 2026 were preliminary and may change."]}